WEBVTT

00:02:27.268 --> 00:02:30.438
into what's called
long-term episodic memory.

00:02:30.479 --> 00:02:33.024
It has to become
an episode in our narrative.

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:37.778
But what if the experience
doesn't even enter short-term memory?

00:02:38.362 --> 00:02:40.781
That's exactly what Alzheimer's does.

00:02:40.823 --> 00:02:41.991
In the beginning,

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:45.453
Alzheimer's impairs
the formation of short-term memory.

00:02:46.037 --> 00:02:48.206
It impairs the growth of the narrative.

00:02:48.247 --> 00:02:52.543
It's as if our stories begin stalling
upon the onset of the disease.

00:02:53.461 --> 00:02:57.298
Eventually, Alzheimer's eats away
at all the long-term memories.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.885
